 # Scroll spike notes
 
-- 0–20%: `.plate` pushes from 1.0 to 1.25 with a scroll-linked drift; `.candle-pool` intensifies.
-- 20–45%: `.letters`, `.tablet`, and `.pile` form far/mid/near parallax layers; `.shaft` crosses the desk with grain.
-- 45–70%: `.daily` uses an inset `clip-path` wipe and `.copy span` enters from its overflow-hidden line wrappers.
-- 70–100%: `.book` cards stagger forward, while their `i` rings fill from the shared scroll progress.
-- Native path: `.scene` animates registered `--p` with `animation-timeline: scroll(root)`. Unsupported browsers use the rAF scroll listener in `spike.js` to write the same property. Reduced motion fixes the finished state and omits dust/loops.
-- Known gaps: this was syntax-checked only; no browser render or console inspection was run in this task. The SVG grain is deliberately procedural and may render differently across engines.
+| Scroll range | Selectors and result |
+| --- | --- |
+| 0–24% | `.plate` pushes in while `.candle-pool` scales and brightens. |
+| 20–58% | `.letters`, `.tablet`, `.pile`, and masked `.shaft` drift on overlapping eased ranges; shaft fades fully by 45%. |
+| 45–70% | `.daily` unrolls; `.line-a .line-content` (52–62%) and `.line-b .line-content` (59–69%) rise independently inside `.line-mask` overflow masks. |
+| 70–97% | `.book` cards and `.ring-fill` layers enter on staggered overlapping ranges; every ring completes. |
+
+Native browsers use individual `scroll(root)` timelines and eased keyframes. Unsupported browsers use the `spike.js` rAF loop to write `--p`, consumed by equivalent fallback ranges. Reduced motion fixes the final composition, removes dust and the inert 500vh journey, and keeps the heading away from the sheet.
+
+| Refuter defect → how closed |
+| --- |
+| 1 line reveal / false notes | Real masks and independent scroll ranges; no transition delay. |
+| 2 heading collision | Upper-right desktop and upper phone safe areas, unchanged in reduced motion. |
+| 3 unequal rings | Fixed clamp box plus `flex:none`. |
+| 4 shaft seam / persistence | Oversized, four-sided masked shaft fades to zero by 45%. |
+| 5 flat cards | Gradient border, restrained lit edge, and grain overlay. |
+| 6 pool/ring paint | Pool uses opacity/transform/filter; fixed conic layer is revealed only by `clip-path`. |
+| 7 sprite placement | Desktop sprites moved onto desk plane; unsuitable phone layers hidden. |
+| 8 pool detaches | Flame-origin coordinate and scale track the camera push. |
+| 9 flat sheet | Shaded roll edge and inset parchment detail. |
+| 10 shadow clipping | Shadow lives on `.copy`; padded masks prevent a visible text box. |
+| 11 dead filter | Removed. |
+| 12 chirpy copy / phone overlap | Study-specific labels replace slogans; phone hides competing layers. |
+| 13 inert reduced scroll / rings | Reduced journey is 100vh and all four rings are complete. |
+
+Known gaps: `node --check spike.js` checks JavaScript syntax only. I cannot render or inspect frames, console output, frame rate, true non-supporting engines, or high-DPR gradient banding in this task.
